    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Comprehensive Guide to the Authentication Module**\n\n### Table of Contents\n\n1. [Introduction](#introduction)\n2. [Overview of the Authentication Module](#overview-of-the-authentication-module)\n3. [Key Concepts](#key-concepts)\n4. [Installation](#installation)\n5. [Configuration](#configuration)\n6. [Dependencies](#dependencies)\n7. [Authentication Flow](#authentication-flow)\n8. [Authentication Scopes](#authentication-scopes)\n9. [Tokens and Refresh Tokens](#tokens-and-refresh-tokens)\n10. [Security Best Practices](#security-best-practices)\n11. [Troubleshooting](#troubleshooting)\n12. [FAQs](#faqs)\n\n### Introduction\n\nThe Authentication module provides a robust and scalable solution for authenticating users and managing access control. This guide provides a comprehensive overview of the module, its key components, and functionality.\n\n### Overview of the Authentication Module\n\nThe Authentication module integrates with your application's existing backend to provide a secure authentication mechanism for users. This module supports multiple authentication mechanisms, including username/password, OAuth, and OpenID Connect.\n\n### Key Concepts\n\n* **User**: A user represents an individual that wants to access your application's resources",
